<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain has no comment on peseta.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain has no comment on peseta.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain said on Friday it had no comment on early talk it was breaking the peseta's rise with sales of the currency against the mark.</p>
<p>&quot;As a matter of policy, we have no comment on these matters,&quot; a Bank of Spain spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>There has been talk since Wednesday that the Bank of Spain has been holding the peseta back through peseta sales.</p>
<p>But earlier the peseta broke through 84.00 per mark for the first time since November and swiftly strengthened to 83.55.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
